# v16 LANE OVERLAY, sourced after v52_reward.env (REWARD_OVERLAY).
#
# WHY (2026-10-25). v13/v14/v15 all ended ~21/40 Town05 eval episodes on a lane
# crossing at 500k while Town02 fell to 1-5/40. Town05 lanes are painted on
# BOTH sides (solid edge line + broken dividers), so the slow straight-road
# drift measured there (~0.85 m off centre in the first ~10 s) is a fault on
# Town05 but runs into an exempt unpainted kerb on Town02. In training a
# crossing is a -10 fine and the car drives on, so on Town05 the policy learned
# to reach goals (0.53-0.63 training success, its best town) while drifting.
#
#   * Lane-centre POTENTIAL doubled (2/1 -> 4/2). Potential shaping telescopes,
#     so a larger one still cannot make an early end cheaper; it only steepens
#     the pull to the centre.
#   * Crossing fine doubled (10 -> 20), both modes: nearer what a crossing costs
#     in the eval, where it ends the episode and forfeits the +50 arrival.
#     Still a fine, not terminal -- terminal crossings failed four times.
export LANE_CENTRE_K=4.0 LANE_HEADING_K=2.0
export LANE_DEPARTURE_PENALTY=20.0
